<main id="main">

  <!-- ======================================================================
       SERVICES HERO
       ======================================================================
       Layout copied from the reference build (rioproperty.co.za/services),
       structure and metrics both:

         - full-bleed image layer, absolutely positioned, scaled on load and
           parallaxed on scroll, under a flat 60% black overlay
         - a text layer pinned over it, min-height 100svh, contents pushed to
           the BOTTOM of that box
         - a 12-column grid holding two small uppercase paragraphs: one at
           columns 1-3, one at columns 8-12 and right-aligned
         - beneath them the display headline at 16vw, built as three ROWS so
           the words can sit at opposite ends of the same line:
               row 1   "What we"                    (left)
               row 2   "Can"          ...      "Do"  (space-between)
               row 3                       "For You" (right)

       ACCESSIBILITY
       The visible rows are decorative duplicates: they are chopped into
       per-character spans by the split engine, which would make a screen
       reader announce them letter by letter. So the rows are aria-hidden and
       a single visually-hidden <h1> carries the real heading text â€” exactly
       what the reference does, and the reason .u-sr-only exists there.

       data-fouc-prevent marks what must stay invisible until fonts are ready
       and the split has run. If JS never runs the head gate never lands and
       all of this renders as a plain static hero. -->
  <section class="hero-svc" data-hero-svc>

    <div class="hero-svc__bg" data-anim-load="scale" data-parallax="trigger"
         data-parallax-start="0" data-parallax-end="20" data-fouc-prevent>
      <img class="hero-svc__img" src="assets/services.png" alt=""
           decoding="async" fetchpriority="high">
      <span class="hero-svc__overlay" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-svc__textWrap">
      <div class="hero-svc__container">
        <div class="hero-svc__layout">

          <div class="hero-svc__paras">
            <div class="hero-svc__parasCol hero-svc__parasCol--left">
              <p class="hero-svc__para" data-split="lines" data-anim-load="lines"
                 data-anim-load-delay="0.25" data-fouc-prevent>Claims<br>Care<br>Compliance</p>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-svc__parasCol hero-svc__parasCol--right">
              <p class="hero-svc__para hero-svc__para--right" data-split="lines"
                 data-anim-load="lines" data-anim-load-delay="0.5" data-fouc-prevent>We
                manage, document and settle crew medical claims
                <span class="hero-svc__nowrap">across the fleet.</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="hero-svc__headingWrap">
            <h1 class="visually-hidden">What we can do for you</h1>

            <div class="hero-svc__row">
              <div class="hero-svc__heading" aria-hidden="true" data-split="chars"
                   data-anim-load="chars" data-fouc-prevent>What we</div>
            </div>

            <div class="hero-svc__row hero-svc__row--split">
              <div class="hero-svc__heading" aria-hidden="true" data-split="chars"
                   data-anim-load="chars" data-fouc-prevent>Can</div>
              <div class="hero-svc__heading hero-svc__heading--end" aria-hidden="true"
                   data-split="chars" data-anim-load="chars"
                   data-anim-load-delay="0.25" data-fouc-prevent>Do</div>
            </div>

            <div class="hero-svc__row hero-svc__row--end">
              <div class="hero-svc__heading hero-svc__heading--end" aria-hidden="true"
                   data-split="chars" data-anim-load="chars"
                   data-anim-load-delay="0.25" data-fouc-prevent>For You</div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       CTA TEXT â€” the bridge between the hero and the service detail
       ======================================================================
       The reference's .cta_text_section, measured off the live site at
       1900px wide:

         h2      52px / 50.232px Â· 600 Â· uppercase   (same face and size as
                                                      the halves headings, so
                                                      the two read as one
                                                      typographic system)
         lede    18px / 27px Â· regular Â· muted grey
         button  16px Â· 600 Â· uppercase Â· accent, with a diagonal arrow
         gaps    32px between heading, lede and button

       It sets up the section that follows: the halves list answers "who are
       you in the case", and this is the sentence that poses the question.

       Animation uses the same generic contract as everything else on the
       page, so js/services-hero.js needs no new code:
         data-anim-scroll="words"  heading, per-word rise
         data-anim-scroll="lines"  lede, per-line rise
         data-anim-scroll="fade"   the button -->
  <section class="cta-text" aria-labelledby="cta-text-h">
    <div class="cta-text__inner">
      <h2 class="cta-text__h" id="cta-text-h"
          data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">It depends who you are in the case</h2>
      <div class="cta-text__bottom">
        <p class="cta-text__lede" data-anim-scroll="lines" data-split="lines">Every
          case looks different depending on where you stand. An owner, a
          crewing manager and the seafarer each need something different from
          the same file &mdash; and we adjust what we do to match.</p>
        <div class="cta-text__cta" data-anim-scroll="fade">
          <a class="cta-text__link" href="contact.html">Get in touch
            <svg class="cta-text__arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                 width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M7.05 16.95 16.95 7.05M16.95 7.05H7.05M16.95 7.05v9.9"
                    stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       SERVICES â€” "it depends who you are in the case"
       ======================================================================
       Layout and motion copied from the reference build
       (rioproperty.co.za/services, its .services_halves_section), measured off
       the live site rather than estimated:

         - each item is a 50/50 flex row, 32px gap, 80px block padding
         - text column is BOTTOM-aligned (justify-content: flex-end) with an
           80px gap between its heading group and its list
         - image is 4:5 and rendered at height:120% with
           object-position:50% 100%, which is the overscan its parallax
           travels through
         - items ALTERNATE: the reference does this at runtime by setting
           order:-1 on the image wrapper of every even item, which is why the
           alternation is invisible in its static HTML. Here it is a CSS class
           (.halves__item--flip) â€” same result, no JS required, and it still
           works if scripting fails.

       Counter-parallax: the text moves 10 -> -10 while the image moves
       -20 -> 15, so the two columns drift against each other as the row
       crosses the viewport. Both are disabled at tablet and below.

       Animation attributes are the same generic contract the hero uses, so
       js/services-hero.js drives this section too with no new code:
         data-anim-scroll="words"  heading, per-word rise
         data-anim-scroll="lines"  subheading, per-line rise
         data-anim-scroll="fade"   the list block
       Unlike the hero's load animations these are scroll-triggered, and they
       replay when scrolled back to â€” matching the reference's
       toggleActions:"none play none reset". -->
  <section class="halves" aria-labelledby="halves-h">
    <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="halves-h">What we do, service by service</h2>

    <article class="halves__item" id="claims" aria-labelledby="claims-h">

      <div class="halves__text" data-parallax="trigger"
           data-parallax-start="10" data-parallax-end="-10"
           data-parallax-disable="tablet">
        <div class="halves__textTop">
          <p class="halves__num">01</p>
          <h2 class="halves__h" id="claims-h" data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">Claims management</h2>
          <p class="halves__sub" data-anim-scroll="lines" data-split="lines">A claim documented from the first hour, so it settles instead of being disputed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="halves__rich" data-anim-scroll="fade">
          <p class="halves__richLead">What you get:</p>
          <ul>
              <li>End-to-end handling from incident to settlement</li>
              <li>Incident documentation and evidence collection from hour one</li>
              <li>Employer negotiation through to final settlement</li>
              <li>Crew injury, illness, and mental health conditions covered</li>
              <li>Handled against maritime law and international compliance standards</li>
              <li>Fraud prevention, policy compliance and dispute mitigation</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="halves__cta" href="contact.html">Ask about claims <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="halves__imageWrap">
        <img class="halves__image" src="assets/services/claims.jpg" alt="A crew member working on the wet deck of a tanker at sea."
             loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1067"
             data-parallax="trigger" data-parallax-start="-20"
             data-parallax-end="15" data-parallax-disable="tablet">
      </div>

    </article>

    <article class="halves__item halves__item--flip" id="advisory" aria-labelledby="advisory-h">

      <div class="halves__text" data-parallax="trigger"
           data-parallax-start="10" data-parallax-end="-10"
           data-parallax-disable="tablet">
        <div class="halves__textTop">
          <p class="halves__num">02</p>
          <h2 class="halves__h" id="advisory-h" data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">Claims advisory &amp; legal</h2>
          <p class="halves__sub" data-anim-scroll="lines" data-split="lines">A defensible position before a case becomes a liability.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="halves__rich" data-anim-scroll="fade">
          <p class="halves__richLead">What you get:</p>
          <ul>
              <li>Structured review of the employer&rsquo;s obligations and medical records</li>
              <li>Collaborative resolution between crew, employer and agents</li>
              <li>Alignment with MLC and ILO standards</li>
              <li>Disputes mediated to fair resolution rather than litigated</li>
              <li>Objective medical evaluation on disability claims</li>
              <li>Beneficiary analysis and confidential life-claims resolution</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="halves__cta" href="contact.html">Ask about advisory <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="halves__imageWrap">
        <img class="halves__image" src="assets/services/advisory.jpg" alt="A lawyer on the telephone reviewing case papers in an office."
             loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1067"
             data-parallax="trigger" data-parallax-start="-20"
             data-parallax-end="15" data-parallax-disable="tablet">
      </div>

    </article>

    <article class="halves__item" id="budgeting" aria-labelledby="budgeting-h">

      <div class="halves__text" data-parallax="trigger"
           data-parallax-start="10" data-parallax-end="-10"
           data-parallax-disable="tablet">
        <div class="halves__textTop">
          <p class="halves__num">03</p>
          <h2 class="halves__h" id="budgeting-h" data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">Medical welfare budgeting</h2>
          <p class="halves__sub" data-anim-scroll="lines" data-split="lines">A crew medical spend you can forecast at budget time and defend at year end.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="halves__rich" data-anim-scroll="fade">
          <p class="halves__richLead">What you get:</p>
          <ul>
              <li>Needs assessment across your whole fleet</li>
              <li>Budgets designed around preventive care and onboard staffing</li>
              <li>Evacuation contingency and telemedicine costs accounted for</li>
              <li>Data-driven forecasting that removes financial surprise</li>
              <li>PEME and vessel-specific audits included</li>
              <li>Built to satisfy global maritime health regulation</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="halves__cta" href="contact.html">Ask about budgeting <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="halves__imageWrap">
        <img class="halves__image" src="assets/services/budgeting.jpg" alt="A budget worksheet of forecast costs being reviewed line by line."
             loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1067"
             data-parallax="trigger" data-parallax-start="-20"
             data-parallax-end="15" data-parallax-disable="tablet">
      </div>

    </article>

    <article class="halves__item halves__item--flip" id="telemedicine" aria-labelledby="tele-h">

      <div class="halves__text" data-parallax="trigger"
           data-parallax-start="10" data-parallax-end="-10"
           data-parallax-disable="tablet">
        <div class="halves__textTop">
          <p class="halves__num">04</p>
          <h2 class="halves__h" id="tele-h" data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">Telemedicine</h2>
          <p class="halves__sub" data-anim-scroll="lines" data-split="lines">A doctor on the line before the master has to make a diversion call alone.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="halves__rich" data-anim-scroll="fade">
          <p class="halves__richLead">What you get:</p>
          <ul>
              <li>24/7 access to licensed doctors and specialists</li>
              <li>Real-time video consultation and remote diagnostics</li>
              <li>Wearable diagnostics supported</li>
              <li>Fewer unnecessary evacuations and costly port diversions</li>
              <li>Every consultation documented against maritime health standards</li>
              <li>Regulatory compliance built into the record</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="halves__cta" href="contact.html">Ask about telemedicine <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="halves__imageWrap">
        <img class="halves__image" src="assets/services/telemedicine.jpg" alt="A clinician in a headset consulting a patient by video call and taking notes."
             loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1600" height="1067"
             data-parallax="trigger" data-parallax-start="-20"
             data-parallax-end="15" data-parallax-disable="tablet">
      </div>

    </article>

  </section>


  <!-- ======================================================================
       HOW WE PROTECT THE CLAIM â€” accordion
       ======================================================================
       The reference's .accordion_services_section, measured off the live
       site at 1900px wide:

         section    padding-block 96px
         row        12-column grid, 16px gutter, 32px block padding
                    col 1     the service icon
                    col 5-7   the heading
                    col 9-11  the disclosure content
                    col 12    the plus/minus toggle
         h3         32px / 37.44px Â· 600 Â· uppercase
         body       16px / 24px
         divider    1px rule above every row, with a brand-coloured highlight
                    that wipes across on hover and stays while open

       The open/close is pure CSS: grid-template-rows 0fr -> 1fr over
       0.75s cubic-bezier(0.625, 0.05, 0, 1), the reference's own easing,
       lifted from the inline <style> block it ships. No height measuring,
       so it animates correctly whatever the content length.

       ACCESSIBILITY â€” this differs from the reference deliberately. The
       reference toggles a data attribute on a <button> with no ARIA at all.
       Here each row is a real <button> carrying aria-expanded and
       aria-controls, and the panel is a labelled region, so the state is
       announced rather than only shown. Keyboard operation comes free with
       the button element.

       Animation uses the same generic contract as the rest of the page:
         data-anim-scroll="scaleX"  the divider rule draws in
         data-anim-scroll="words"   heading, per-word rise
         data-anim-scroll="fade"    the icons -->
  <section class="acc" aria-labelledby="acc-h">
    <div class="acc__head">
      <p class="acc__eyebrow">How we protect the claim</p>
      <h2 class="acc__title" id="acc-h" data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">Fraud prevention and cost safeguards</h2>
      <p class="acc__lede" data-anim-scroll="lines" data-split="lines">Once a
        hospital learns an employer is paying, prices move. These are the
        specific mechanisms that keep a claim honest.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="acc__wrap" data-accordion-close-siblings="true">
      <ul class="acc__list">
        <li class="acc__item" data-accordion-status="not-active">
          <div class="acc__divider" data-anim-scroll="scaleX">
            <span class="acc__dividerHi"></span>
          </div>
          <button class="acc__row" type="button" data-accordion-toggle
                  aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-panel-1" id="acc-btn-1">
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--icon" data-anim-scroll="fade">
              <svg class="acc__icon" viewBox="0 0 36 36" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 3c-5 0-9 4-9 9 0 6.6 9 21 9 21s9-14.4 9-21c0-5-4-9-9-9Zm0 12.5a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 0-7 3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/></svg>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--title">
              <span class="acc__h" data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">Field verification</span>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--body">
              <span class="acc__content" id="acc-panel-1" role="region"
                    aria-labelledby="acc-btn-1">
                <span class="acc__contentInner">
                  <span class="acc__p">Local field agents, geo-tagged medical visit logs and time-stamped records &mdash; so a claim can be checked against what actually happened, not just what was billed.</span>
                  <span class="acc__lead">Why it matters:</span>
                  <span class="acc__p">A claim is verified against the visit, not just against the invoice.</span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--toggle" data-anim-scroll="fade">
              <span class="acc__plus" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="acc__plusLine"></span>
                <span class="acc__plusLine acc__plusLine--v"></span>
              </span>
            </span>
          </button>
        </li>
        <li class="acc__item" data-accordion-status="not-active">
          <div class="acc__divider" data-anim-scroll="scaleX">
            <span class="acc__dividerHi"></span>
          </div>
          <button class="acc__row" type="button" data-accordion-toggle
                  aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-panel-2" id="acc-btn-2">
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--icon" data-anim-scroll="fade">
              <svg class="acc__icon" viewBox="0 0 36 36" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 33V13l12-7 12 7v20" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/><path d="M14 33V21h8v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/><path d="M18 9v6M15 12h6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--title">
              <span class="acc__h" data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">Tiered hospital empanelment</span>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--body">
              <span class="acc__content" id="acc-panel-2" role="region"
                    aria-labelledby="acc-btn-2">
                <span class="acc__contentInner">
                  <span class="acc__p">A centralised provider-selection policy covering accreditation, emergency response time, treatment quality and pricing transparency &mdash; reviewed and audited periodically.</span>
                  <span class="acc__lead">Why it matters:</span>
                  <span class="acc__p">Reviewed and audited periodically, so the network stays honest over time.</span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--toggle" data-anim-scroll="fade">
              <span class="acc__plus" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="acc__plusLine"></span>
                <span class="acc__plusLine acc__plusLine--v"></span>
              </span>
            </span>
          </button>
        </li>
        <li class="acc__item" data-accordion-status="not-active">
          <div class="acc__divider" data-anim-scroll="scaleX">
            <span class="acc__dividerHi"></span>
          </div>
          <button class="acc__row" type="button" data-accordion-toggle
                  aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-panel-3" id="acc-btn-3">
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--icon" data-anim-scroll="fade">
              <svg class="acc__icon" viewBox="0 0 36 36" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="4" width="22" height="28" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/><path d="M12 12h12M12 18h12M12 24h7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--title">
              <span class="acc__h" data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">Treatment-guideline library</span>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--body">
              <span class="acc__content" id="acc-panel-3" role="region"
                    aria-labelledby="acc-btn-3">
                <span class="acc__contentInner">
                  <span class="acc__p">A standard treatment-guideline reference for the most common seafarer injuries and conditions, so proposed treatment can be checked against a known baseline.</span>
                  <span class="acc__lead">Why it matters:</span>
                  <span class="acc__p">Proposed treatment can be checked against a known baseline before it is approved.</span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--toggle" data-anim-scroll="fade">
              <span class="acc__plus" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="acc__plusLine"></span>
                <span class="acc__plusLine acc__plusLine--v"></span>
              </span>
            </span>
          </button>
        </li>
        <li class="acc__item" data-accordion-status="not-active">
          <div class="acc__divider" data-anim-scroll="scaleX">
            <span class="acc__dividerHi"></span>
          </div>
          <button class="acc__row" type="button" data-accordion-toggle
                  aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-panel-4" id="acc-btn-4">
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--icon" data-anim-scroll="fade">
              <svg class="acc__icon" viewBox="0 0 36 36" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="7" width="28" height="22" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/><path d="M10 23v-6M17 23v-10M24 23v-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--title">
              <span class="acc__h" data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">Cost-intelligence dashboard</span>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--body">
              <span class="acc__content" id="acc-panel-4" role="region"
                    aria-labelledby="acc-btn-4">
                <span class="acc__contentInner">
                  <span class="acc__p">Treatment cost data by region and condition, pre-treatment cost estimates and approvals, and automated flags on cost deviation.</span>
                  <span class="acc__lead">Why it matters:</span>
                  <span class="acc__p">Automated flags on cost deviation catch a moving price before it is paid.</span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--toggle" data-anim-scroll="fade">
              <span class="acc__plus" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="acc__plusLine"></span>
                <span class="acc__plusLine acc__plusLine--v"></span>
              </span>
            </span>
          </button>
        </li>
        <li class="acc__item" data-accordion-status="not-active">
          <div class="acc__divider" data-anim-scroll="scaleX">
            <span class="acc__dividerHi"></span>
          </div>
          <button class="acc__row" type="button" data-accordion-toggle
                  aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-panel-5" id="acc-btn-5">
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--icon" data-anim-scroll="fade">
              <svg class="acc__icon" viewBox="0 0 36 36" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="15" cy="15" r="9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/><path d="m22 22 8 8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M11 15h8M15 11v8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--title">
              <span class="acc__h" data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">Second opinions</span>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--body">
              <span class="acc__content" id="acc-panel-5" role="region"
                    aria-labelledby="acc-btn-5">
                <span class="acc__contentInner">
                  <span class="acc__p">Where a proposed treatment is unusual for the region, our panel reviews it before it is approved.</span>
                  <span class="acc__lead">Why it matters:</span>
                  <span class="acc__p">An unnecessary or overpriced procedure is stopped before it happens, not disputed on the invoice afterwards.</span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--toggle" data-anim-scroll="fade">
              <span class="acc__plus" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="acc__plusLine"></span>
                <span class="acc__plusLine acc__plusLine--v"></span>
              </span>
            </span>
          </button>
        </li>
        <li class="acc__item" data-accordion-status="not-active">
          <div class="acc__divider" data-anim-scroll="scaleX">
            <span class="acc__dividerHi"></span>
          </div>
          <button class="acc__row" type="button" data-accordion-toggle
                  aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-panel-6" id="acc-btn-6">
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--icon" data-anim-scroll="fade">
              <svg class="acc__icon" viewBox="0 0 36 36" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6" y="5" width="24" height="26" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/><path d="M13 3v4M23 3v4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="m12 19 4 4 8-8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/></svg>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--title">
              <span class="acc__h" data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">Single digital case record</span>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--body">
              <span class="acc__content" id="acc-panel-6" role="region"
                    aria-labelledby="acc-btn-6">
                <span class="acc__contentInner">
                  <span class="acc__p">One platform instead of siloed PEME, ship and hospital records &mdash; nothing gets lost or contradicted between stakeholders.</span>
                  <span class="acc__lead">Why it matters:</span>
                  <span class="acc__p">Nothing gets lost or contradicted between stakeholders.</span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="acc__col acc__col--toggle" data-anim-scroll="fade">
              <span class="acc__plus" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="acc__plusLine"></span>
                <span class="acc__plusLine acc__plusLine--v"></span>
              </span>
            </span>
          </button>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       ALSO AVAILABLE â€” OHS and medico-legal
       ======================================================================
       Built on the reference's .laws_home_grid pattern (its homepage), which
       is the closest thing it has to a peer-cards block: a grid whose 1px
       GAP is the only separator, with a background layer showing through the
       gaps as hairlines. Measured off the live site:

         grid      1px column gap, 0 row gap, cards on #FFFEFC
         card      padding 32px 18px
         body      16px / 24px
         hairline  a 1px rule inside each card, above its foot

       Its 3 columns become 2 here, because there are two services. The
       services page has no equivalent section in the reference (it goes
       accordion -> CTA -> contact form), so this adapts an existing pattern
       rather than inventing one.

       Its animation stack, reproduced:
         mask-diagonal  the backing layer wipes in from the top-left corner
         scaleX         the wrapper and each card's inner rule draw outward
         lines          the card text rises line by line -->
  <section class="laws" aria-labelledby="laws-h">
    <div class="laws__head">
      <p class="laws__eyebrow">Also available</p>
      <h2 class="laws__title" id="laws-h" data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">Occupational health &amp; safety, and medico-legal services</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="laws__outer">
      <!-- The layer that shows through the 1px gaps. It carries the diagonal
           wipe, so the hairlines draw themselves in from the corner. -->
      <div class="laws__bg" data-anim-scroll="mask-diagonal" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <div class="laws__grid" data-anim-scroll="children-fade">
        <div class="laws__card" data-anim-target>
          <span class="laws__hi" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="laws__inner">
            <h3 class="laws__cardH" data-anim-scroll="lines" data-split="lines">Occupational Health &amp; Safety</h3>
            <p class="laws__p" data-anim-scroll="lines" data-split="lines">Maritime
              safety audits, PEME-related audits and vessel-specific audits
              &mdash; focused on preventing workplace injury and ensuring
              compliance with international safety standards.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="laws__rule" data-anim-scroll="scaleX" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="laws__card" data-anim-target>
          <span class="laws__hi" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="laws__inner">
            <h3 class="laws__cardH" data-anim-scroll="lines" data-split="lines">Medico-Legal Services</h3>
            <p class="laws__p" data-anim-scroll="lines" data-split="lines">Combining
              medical and legal expertise: advice on injury claims, maritime
              regulations and dispute resolution &mdash; protecting clients
              from legal risk while upholding standards of care.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="laws__rule" data-anim-scroll="scaleX" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       HOW A CASE RUNS â€” auto-advancing pairs over a full-bleed image
       ======================================================================
       Layout follows the supplied reference: a photographic background with
       text sitting at the BOTTOM LEFT and BOTTOM RIGHT, and dot indicators
       centred beneath. The eight steps are shown two at a time, so the pair
       reads as "this happens, then this" and the section advances through
       four slides on its own.

       Timing: 5s per slide, paused while the pointer is over the section and
       whenever the section is off-screen, so it is never advancing where it
       cannot be seen. Dots are real buttons, so the sequence is operable
       rather than only decorative.

       Motion vocabulary is the page's own: the outgoing pair fades and drops,
       the incoming pair rises, and the background holds a slow scale so the
       image is never static behind changing text. -->
  <section class="proc" id="process" aria-labelledby="proc-h"
           data-proc data-proc-interval="5000">
    <div class="proc__bg" data-parallax="trigger"
         data-parallax-start="-8" data-parallax-end="8"
         data-parallax-disable="tablet">
      <img class="proc__img" src="assets/services/process-bg.jpg" alt=""
           loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="2000" height="1200">
      <span class="proc__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="proc__inner">
      <div class="proc__head">
        <p class="proc__eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2 class="proc__title" id="proc-h" data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">One case, eight steps, one point of contact</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="proc__stage" data-proc-stage>
        <div class="proc__slide is-active" data-proc-slide="0">
          <div class="proc__col proc__col--left">
            <span class="proc__num">01</span>
            <h3 class="proc__h">The case opens</h3>
            <p class="proc__p">A seafarer needs medical support. One number, answered at any hour.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="proc__col proc__col--right">
            <span class="proc__num">02</span>
            <h3 class="proc__h">A dedicated CMS is assigned</h3>
            <p class="proc__p">One named Case Management Specialist becomes the single liaison between employer, agent, hospital and patient.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="proc__slide" data-proc-slide="1" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="proc__col proc__col--left">
            <span class="proc__num">03</span>
            <h3 class="proc__h">Our SME panel reviews</h3>
            <p class="proc__p">Specialists assess urgency, complexity and treatment options &mdash; decisions backed by expertise, not guesswork.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="proc__col proc__col--right">
            <span class="proc__num">04</span>
            <h3 class="proc__h">Hospital selection, scored</h3>
            <p class="proc__p">A multi-parameter index ranks facilities on expertise, success rate, cost, accessibility and accreditation.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="proc__slide" data-proc-slide="2" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="proc__col proc__col--left">
            <span class="proc__num">05</span>
            <h3 class="proc__h">Treatment plan approved</h3>
            <p class="proc__p">Plan, expected outcome and financial estimate agreed with the employer before treatment begins.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="proc__col proc__col--right">
            <span class="proc__num">06</span>
            <h3 class="proc__h">International payment handled</h3>
            <p class="proc__p">The hospital is paid directly, documented and compliant with global financial regulations &mdash; no crew member out of pocket.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="proc__slide" data-proc-slide="3" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="proc__col proc__col--left">
            <span class="proc__num">07</span>
            <h3 class="proc__h">Recovery monitored</h3>
            <p class="proc__p">Oversight continues through rehabilitation and follow-up, with the employer updated throughout.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="proc__col proc__col--right">
            <span class="proc__num">08</span>
            <h3 class="proc__h">Fitness report &amp; dashboard</h3>
            <p class="proc__p">A treating doctor&rsquo;s fitness-to-work report, plus real-time updates and analytics on one secure dashboard.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="proc__dots" role="group" aria-label="Case steps">
        <button class="proc__dot is-active" type="button" data-proc-dot="0" aria-label="Step pair 1 of 4" aria-current="true"></button><button class="proc__dot" type="button" data-proc-dot="1" aria-label="Step pair 2 of 4"></button><button class="proc__dot" type="button" data-proc-dot="2" aria-label="Step pair 3 of 4"></button><button class="proc__dot" type="button" data-proc-dot="3" aria-label="Step pair 4 of 4"></button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Road ahead â€” HIDDEN.
       Kept in the markup rather than deleted so the copy is not lost, but
       `hidden` keeps it out of the layout AND out of the accessibility tree.
       Delete this wrapper comment and the hidden attribute to restore it. -->
  <section class="inner-section inner-section--sunken" aria-labelledby="road-h" hidden>
    <div class="shell">
      <header class="inner-section__head">
        <p class="eyebrow">The road ahead</p>
        <h2 class="section-title" id="road-h">What's coming</h2>
        <p class="inner-section__lede">Forward-looking initiatives, not yet live - shared here so you know what to expect.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="roadmap-grid">
        <div class="roadmap-card">
          <span class="roadmap-card__tag">Planned</span>
          <h4>Global expansion</h4>
          <p>Offices in Italy, USA and the UK, extending support for maritime clients worldwide.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="roadmap-card">
          <span class="roadmap-card__tag">Planned</span>
          <h4>Customised digital solutions</h4>
          <p>Branded mobile applications tailored to each client, streamlining healthcare management.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="roadmap-card">
          <span class="roadmap-card__tag">Planned</span>
          <h4>Strategic growth in India</h4>
          <p>10 PEME centres across key Indian cities for standardised pre-employment medical examinations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="roadmap-card">
          <span class="roadmap-card__tag">Planned</span>
          <h4>Onboard healthcare integration</h4>
          <p>Software installed in each client's ship clinic for real-time record-keeping and health monitoring.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ======================================================================
       CLOSING CTA
       ======================================================================
       Built on the reference's final .cta_text_section, measured live at
       1900px:

         ground   near-white, NOT a filled colour band
         h2       52px / 50.232px - 600 - uppercase
         sub      24px / 36px - uppercase - brand colour
         body     18px / 27px - muted grey
         layout   two columns, 8 and 4 of 12, 16px gutter
         gaps     32px between heading, subheading and the two-column row

       Shape of the copy follows the reference too: a flat statement as the
       heading, the "and here is why" line beneath it, then the explanation
       and the link set off to the right. -->
  <section class="close-cta" aria-labelledby="close-cta-h">
    <div class="close-cta__inner">
      <h2 class="close-cta__h" id="close-cta-h"
          data-anim-scroll="words" data-split="words">We don&rsquo;t publish our (hundreds of) case outcomes.</h2>

      <div class="close-cta__bottom">
        <div class="close-cta__left">
          <p class="close-cta__sub" data-anim-scroll="lines" data-split="lines">Every
            case is confidential, and that&rsquo;s the point.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="close-cta__right">
          <p class="close-cta__body" data-anim-scroll="lines" data-split="lines">Numbers
            are easy to publish. Crew medical files are not. Tell us your fleet
            profile and the cases you are carrying, and we&rsquo;ll show you
            exactly how we would handle them.</p>

          <div class="close-cta__ctaWrap" data-anim-scroll="fade">
            <a class="close-cta__link" href="contact.html">Get in touch
              <svg class="close-cta__arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                   width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M7.05 16.95 16.95 7.05M16.95 7.05H7.05M16.95 7.05v9.9"
                      stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/>
              </svg>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

